    pooled substrate 6,528,330 bars / 5,466 sessions [4s]

==============================================================================================================================
=== 0. CAUSALITY ASSERTION - does any volume driver see its own session's afternoon?
==============================================================================================================================
    `CORRECTION` the first version of this check corrupted EVERY traded session at once and
    then asked whether each session's driver moved. Of course it moved - session i's window
    covers sessions i-60..i-1, most of which were also corrupted. The check fired on all
    three drivers and the DEFECT WAS THE CHECK. Replaced with two tests that have teeth:
    (a) a window identity, and (b) a SINGLE-session perturbation.

    V_CLOSE_SHARE        window == mean(raw[i-60:i]): True    own session cannot move it: True    NEXT session does move (teeth): True 
    V_LASTHOUR_RATIO     window == mean(raw[i-60:i]): True    own session cannot move it: True    NEXT session does move (teeth): True 
    SESSION_VOL_LEVEL    window == mean(raw[i-60:i]): True    own session cannot move it: True    NEXT session does move (teeth): True 
    PRICE_LEVEL uses the 09:31 OPEN of the traded session, known at 11:48. CAL_YEAR and
    TIME_IDX are pure calendar and are NULL DRIVERS ONLY (directive section 31).
    PASS.

